#: ../../../library/tkinter.systray.rst:2
msgid ":mod:`!tkinter.systray` --- System tray icon and notifications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/tkinter.systray.rst:7
msgid "**Source code:** :source:`Lib/tkinter/systray.py`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/tkinter.systray.rst:13
msgid ""
"The :mod:`!tkinter.systray` module provides the :class:`SysTrayIcon` class "
"as an interface to the system tray (or taskbar) icon, and the :func:`notify` "
"function which sends a desktop notification. They require Tk 8.7/9.0 or "
"newer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/tkinter.systray.rst:18
msgid "Only one system tray icon is supported per Tcl interpreter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/tkinter.systray.rst:22
msgid "The class implementing the system tray icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/tkinter.systray.rst:24
msgid ""
"With *exists* false (the default), a new icon is created; creating a second "
"one raises :exc:`~tkinter.TclError`. With *exists* true, the instance refers "
"to the already-existing icon instead of creating one, reconfiguring it with "
"any given options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/tkinter.systray.rst:29
msgid "The supported configuration options are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/tkinter.systray.rst:31
msgid ""
"*image* --- the image displayed in the system tray (required when creating "
"an icon). On Windows, it must be a :class:`!PhotoImage`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/tkinter.systray.rst:34
msgid "*text* --- the text displayed in the tooltip of the icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/tkinter.systray.rst:35
msgid ""
"*button1* --- a callback that is called without arguments when the icon is "
"clicked with the left mouse button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/tkinter.systray.rst:37
msgid ""
"*button3* --- a callback that is called without arguments when the icon is "
"clicked with the right mouse button."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/tkinter.systray.rst:43
msgid ""
"Query or modify the options of the system tray icon. With no arguments, "
"return a dict of all option values. With a string argument, return the value "
"of that option. Otherwise, set the given options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/tkinter.systray.rst:50
msgid "Return the value of the given option of the system tray icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/tkinter.systray.rst:54
msgid "Return whether the system tray icon exists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/tkinter.systray.rst:58
msgid "Destroy the system tray icon. A new icon can be created afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/tkinter.systray.rst:63
msgid "Send a desktop notification with the given title and message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../library/tkinter.systray.rst:68
msgid ""
"Send a desktop notification with the given title and message without "
"creating a system tray icon first. On Windows, sending a notification "
"requires an existing system tray icon, which is also displayed in the "
"notification; use the :meth:`SysTrayIcon.notify` method instead."
msgstr ""
